--TEST--
the name after `extend` must be a class, an interface or an enum: a `Core` attribute and a `type` alias are neither, and each block is refused at its target (`rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

type Id = int;

extend Core\Deprecated as DeprecatedTools {
    public function label(): string {
        return "old";
    }
}

extend Id as IdTools {
    public function label(): string {
        return "id";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0336]: `Core\Deprecated` is not a class, an interface or an enum, and an `extend` block extends one of these
%A
error[E0336]: `Shop\Id` is a type alias, and an `extend` block extends a class, an interface or an enum
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
